content.text:
Yes, I ran all 8 examples. Each one matched its expected rows and cycle count exactly, and I recorded the cycle cost of every instruction.

`notes/examples.md` has, for each program, what it computes, its cycles and where the cost goes, and where it wastes work. It ends with the patterns that recur across the examples:
- unused columns and dead instructions;
- every column carried through each join;
- filters applied late;
- sorts that change nothing;
- quadratic self-joins used for per-group stats.

The waste notes come from reading the programs alongside the measured costs. I haven't rewritten any example and re-measured, and the two items marked *(needs proof)* still need confirming.

